    "tranche": "T4",
    "tranche_reason": "Uses SAM as a training method and compares it with SGD and ASAM while developing infoSAM. It does not test the listed claim versions or measure the training–test gap.",
    "gate_note": "The paper reports test accuracies for SGD, SAM, ASAM, and infoSAM on CIFAR-10 and CIFAR-100. Baseline results for SGD, SAM, and ASAM are recorded below as findings about generalization not covered by a listed version. The proposed infoSAM results are comparisons of the study's own method and are not extracted as rows. ImageNet and label-noise comparisons are described in text or figures but do not provide extractable baseline values for the listed versions.",
    "test_reason": "The study uses the flatness–generalization rationale to develop and evaluate infoSAM. It reports optimizer test accuracies, but does not measure magnitude-aware sharpness, training–test gaps, or rankings against norm and margin measures required by V7. Its other experiments also do not test V1–V8. ASAM adapts adversarial perturbations, rather than providing the adaptive parameter-update comparison named in V4.",
    "authors_conclusion": "The record's paraphrase is accurate: the authors present preSAM as a unifying framework and convergence analysis, and conclude that infoSAM addresses adversarial model degradation and improves benchmark generalization. This conclusion concerns their proposed optimizer, rather than a direct test of V1–V8.",
    "recipe": "different",
    "recipe_differences": "Develops a preconditioned SAM framework and infoSAM; compares SAM variants using ordinary test accuracy, without testing the listed claim versions or measuring training–test gaps.",
    "method_sensitivity": "The authors report that ASAM underperforms SAM with the same ρ, and state that ASAM requires a larger ρ for comparable performance.",
    "fits_no_version": [
      {
        "finding": "SAM has higher test accuracy than SGD in all eight CIFAR architecture–dataset combinations. ASAM is below SAM but above SGD in every combination when assigned SAM's perturbation radius. These are recipe comparisons; SGD uses weight decay 5×10−4 while SAM and ASAM use 1×10−3.",
        "proposed_claim": "SAM and ASAM training recipes can improve CIFAR test accuracy over SGD, with performance sensitive to perturbation-radius selection.",
